    "summary": "The configurator can't fit five drawers in one hex base, so this is a compromise. What's on screen now is one north-half hex base with a single drawer in its cut face (2 nodes; the parts budget reads 5). Drawers only go on the cut face of a half base. A full base takes none, a quarter base takes none and a half base takes one. I also tried a single 3-storey half base. It only offered 3 drawers, one per storey, and the extra storeys stack on top, which the brief rules out. I removed it. I didn't run capOpenFaces or lockJoints, because the brief says nothing else should be added. Three outer faces could take end caps but are left open. check_build shows no rule errors and the meshes are clear.",
